    (uuid "5060b3b0-0b28-5d72-9b46-f384618dbdae"))
  (text "Forward buffers use destination supplies and Ioff protection. Return buffers use MCU +3V3 and per-device CS.\nNo simultaneous SPI2 chip selects. ADC2 conversions/configuration restart after every ACT power/sleep cycle.\nDriver nFAULT pull-up is in the AVDD domain: do not pull it low from an unpowered MCU (test-mode risk).\nAt AVDD = 3.1V, 10k/100k fault bias is 2.82V, above TI's 2.2V power-up requirement.\nBuffers isolate power-off domains; power-ramp/brownout behavior and 20MHz timing still require bench validation."
    (at 20 249 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.2 1.2))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid "9e817aeb-1155-5fde-8039-e09677b45619"))
  (embedded_fonts no))
